.nh
.TH "PB-SETUP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-setup - Set up this machine for Paperboat


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb setup [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Enroll this machine in the signed-in account and set it up: create its Inbox, install the
running executable as the Paperboat service, and register its managed SSH target. Sign in with
pb login first. Flags choose the machine name and which incoming services it accepts, and
--ssh-port names the loopback port of the SSH server already running here (default 22). A recovery key is written only where
--recovery-output says; store it carefully.

.PP
On Windows, setup prepares OpenSSH first and may ask for administrator approval. On macOS a
hostname such as Name.local is shortened to its first label for the machine name.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--file-receive\fP[=true]
	accept native Inbox transfers

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for setup

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--managed-ssh\fP[=true]
	accept managed SSH tools

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	machine name

.PP
\fB--preview-tunnel\fP[=true]
	serve previews and tunnels

.PP
\fB--recovery-output\fP=""
	new absolute file for the account recovery key

.PP
\fB--ssh-port\fP=22
	existing loopback sshd port

.PP
\fB--state-root\fP=""
	runtime state directory

.PP
\fB--terminal\fP[=true]
	accept Paperboat terminal and exec


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb setup --name studio
  pb setup --name studio --ssh-port 2222 --managed-ssh=false
  pb setup --recovery-output /root/pb-recovery.txt --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
